      "text": "Third night in the village. The barkeep has said eleven words to me, four of them 'wine'. I have the castle's outline drawn from three sides now, and a list of the windows that are lit. One is lit every night: high in the east tower, a library or I am no judge of shelving. Tomorrow I go up the road. If anyone finds this, send it to the college at Mirabar, where they still have my good pen. Tell them I was right. Tell them he knows I am reading. A. M."
